  "title": "CropCopter",
  "description": "A Fabric mod for Minecraft 26.2 that adds automated farming drones. Build terminals, load them with drones + seeds + fuel, and the drones fly out to plant and harvest your fields for you",
  "body": "A Fabric mod for Minecraft 26.2 that adds automated farming drones. Build terminals, load them with drones + seeds + fuel, and the drones fly out to plant and harvest your fields for you\n\n|Features|\n\nTwo drone types that fly out (~10 blocks/second), do their ~0.5s job, and return: Farming Drones plant empty farmland, Harvester Drones reap fully-grown crops.\n\nTwo terminals + a chest: Farming Drones work from a Drone Terminal (seeds/fuel + inventory GUI); Harvester Drones work from a separate Harvester Terminal and deposit produce into an adjacent Produce Chest.\n\nA full auto-farm needs both terminals + a produce chest — add hoppers to route seeds back for a self-sustaining loop.\n\nUp to 4 of each drone type per terminal, working in parallel. More drones = faster coverage.\n\nUpgradable Drone Terminal: 3 seed rows (9/18/27 slots); unlock rows with the Terminal Upgrade item.\n\n42-block work radius around each terminal.\n\nTwo fuel options: any furnace fuel (coal, etc.) or a long-lasting custom Drone Battery. Fuel is spent per drone, per action, with a live fuel bar per drone in the terminal GUI — running more drones costs proportionally more fuel, and idle drones burn none.\n\nRemote control: a Control Panel block + a Linker item let you link terminals and open any of them remotely from the panel.\n\nDrones visibly carry the seed/crop they're transporting.\n\nCore crops: wheat seeds, potatoes, carrots, beetroot seeds.\n\nContents drop when the chest is broken; items appear in a dedicated CropCopter creative tab.\n\nreport any bugs or ideas to add to the mod to Cropcopterreport@gmail.com\n(CLEANER CONTENT COMING)\n    \n",
